Z||000001||GT Bastard||07-25-2000||12:29 AM||||Just a quick note about your sig.... ALL Fiero's had the "H.O." engine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||07-25-2000||12:55 AM||||Where did you get your info?  Everywhere I read, Pontiac put in the 135 HP V6 in 87-88 V6 Fieros.  The high-output versions were only put in 1985-1986 V6 Fieros.  The high-output versions have larger valve openings.  I guess they switched to the other engines to conserve fuel........<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||07-25-2000||01:28 AM||||Engines: all ohv V-6, 173 cid/2837 cc; 1984-86: 140 bhp @ 5200 rpm, 170 lbs-ft @ 3600 rpm; 1987-88: 135 bhp @ 4400 rpm, 165 lbs-ft @ 3600 rpm<P>Source:  World Book of Sports Cars, Page 251-252<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shiner||07-25-2000||01:29 AM||||No, 86SE, The Bastard is right.  ALL V6 equipped Fieros came with the "High Output" 2.8 V6.  The "standard output", if you will, was put in things like J cars and such.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||07-25-2000||04:35 AM||||The only difference is that the 87-88 Fiero's were tested at a lower RPM than the 85-86, to meet federal noise requirements or something of that nature.  therefore the 5 hp difference.<P>1984-86: 140 bhp @ 5200 rpm<BR>1987-88: 135 bhp @ 4400 rpm<P>I don't know why the difference in torque, though.  Could have been some tuning changes in the ECM..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||07-25-2000||06:45 AM||||To the best of my knowledge, all V6 Fieros had the bigger valved HO engine. The difference in torque is measuring it at a different rpm too, except you produce the max torque in the mid-range, so if you measure it at a slightly higher rpm, you're past the peak and the torque readings will start dropping.||||reg||1
Z||000007||b lo 0||07-25-2000||09:23 AM||||The point is, he put H O in his sig because he wanted to.  Nuff said.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||12
Z||000008||KnightRyder31||07-25-2000||12:46 PM||||84 never had a 6cyl HO engine...it had a L4 Duke, LO engine.||||reg||1
